of a new strain of hepatitis E virus from an outbreak in Namibia in 1995.</article-title><source>J Gen Virol</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>85</volume>:<fpage>89</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>95</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1099/vir.0.19587-0</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14718623</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Buisson</surname> <given-names>Y</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Grandadam</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Nicand</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Cheval</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>van Cuyck-Gandre</surname> <given-names>H</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Innis</surname> <given-names>B</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Identification of a novel hepatitis E virus in Nigeria.</article-title><source>J Gen Virol</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>81</volume>:<fpage>903</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10725415</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>